          %h2#warning Warning
          %p
            The term ‘topological category’ is traditional, and comes from the frequent examples in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            %em not
            mean an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal category
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            (a
            = succeed ")!" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topologically+enriched+category"} topologically enriched category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groupoid"} topological groupoid
            is not taken by this tradition; indeed, the only groupoid that is a topological category over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+category"} trivial
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em topological category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"} concrete category
            with nice features matching the ability to form
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+topology"} weak
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+topology"} strong
            topologies in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#default_version Default version
          %p
            Most generally, the definition relates to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon C \to D
            (such as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            to
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle"} bundle
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is in fact
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            satisfying the properties described belows is called a
            %em topological construct
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Preuss"} (Preuss)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            will be
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+categories"} large categories
          %p
            By a
            %em space
            we will mean an object of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %em algebra
            we will mean an object of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %em map
            we will mean a morphism in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %em homomorphism
            we will mean a morphism in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
