          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The name ‘topological category’ comes from these examples from point-set
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              %ul
                %li
                  the category
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                  of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
                %li
                  the category of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence+spaces"} convergence spaces
                  (or of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudotopological+space"} pseudotopological
                  or of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopological+space"} pretopological
                  spaces),
                %li
                  the category of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+spaces"} uniform spaces
                  or of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+spaces"} Cauchy spaces
                %li lots more in this vein.
            %li
              %p
                In contrast, the category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locales"} locales
                is
                %em not
                topological over
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
                %em spatial
                locales (equivalent to the category of
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+spaces"} sober spaces
            %li
              %p
                Also, the category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
                is not topological but most categories of
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+space"} generalized smooth space
            %li
              %p
                Outside of topology, the category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+spaces"} measurable spaces
                is topological over
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %li
              %p
                The category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groups"} topological groups
                is topological over
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+spaces"} topological vector spaces
                is topological over
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℝ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
          %h2#further_properties Further properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is topological over
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Cat
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat/D
            %li
              %p
                In particular, a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective
                or
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflective
                subcategory of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is topological, as long as the reflectors or coreflectors become
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphisms"} identity morphisms
                in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %li
              %p
                The forgetful functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon C \to D
                is not only faithful but also (because every algebra must have an initial/indiscrete topology determined by the empty source)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+functor"} essentially surjective
                (in fact surjective on the nose for the non-weak definitions). Thus it is never
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+functor"} full
                (except in the trivial case where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                is an
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+category"} complete
                or
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+category"} cocomplete
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+category"} total
                or cototal, then so is
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid+functor"} solid functor
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mono-complete+category"} mono-complete
                or epi-cocomplete, then so is
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-powered+category"} well-powered
                or co-well-powered, then so is
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                has a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+structure+for+sinks"} factorization structure for sinks
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo ,
                        %mi M
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E,M)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                has one
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ,
                        %mi M
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E',M')
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M'
                is the collection of morphisms in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                lying over
                = succeed "-morphisms" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E'
                the collection of
                %em final
                sinks in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                lying over
                = succeed "-sinks" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+factorization+systems"} orthogonal factorization systems
                along
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibrations"} Grothendieck fibrations
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"} concrete
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                has a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generator"} generator
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is concrete over
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %li
              %p
                In particular, if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a concrete category that is complete, cocomplete, well powered, and well copowered.
          %h2#functors Functors
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon C\to C'
                between topological concrete categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/D
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C'/D
                with the same base category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                preserves initial lifts iff it is right adjoint. It preserves final lifts iff it is left adjoint.
            %li
              %p
                More generally: If a functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon C\to C'
                between topological concrete categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/D
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi D
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C'/D'
                with different base categories lying over a functor
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mn 0
                        %mo :
                        %mi D
                        %mo →
                        %mi D
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_0: D\to D'
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                is right (left) adjoint, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_0
                is right (left) adjoint and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                preserves initial (final) lifts. A partial converse holds: If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_0
                is right (left) adjoint to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_0
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                preserves initial (final) lifts, then there is functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                lying over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_0
                so that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                is right (left) adjoint to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_0
          %h2#special_cases Special cases
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is any algebra, then there is a
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+space"} discrete space
                over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                induced by the empty family of maps. Similarly, we have an
                %em indiscrete space
                with the final structure induced by no maps. This defines functors
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi disc
                      %mo ,
                      %mi indisc
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi D
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} disc, indisc\colon D \to C
                that are respectively left and right
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoints
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %li
              %p
                Suppose that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                has an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mn 0
                          %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0_D
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 0
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0_C
                over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 0
                        %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0_D
                is initial in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                is terminal in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
                More generally, suppose that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                has
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
                or
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
                (indexed by whichever
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinal+number"} cardinalities
                you may wish to consider). Then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                also has (co)products, lying over the (co)products in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %li
              %p
                More general
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
                are constructed in a similar way. However, it is
                %em not
                typically the case that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/created+limit"} creates
                (co)limits in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                because creation of a limit requires that every preimage of the limiting cone is limiting. This fails for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Top
                      %mo →
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U: \mathrm{Top} \to \mathrm{Set}
                since we can coarsen the topology on the limit vertex to obtain a counterexample.
            %li
              %p
                If a single algebra
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                has been given the structure of several spaces, then there are a
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supremum"} supremum
                structure and an
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infimum"} infimum
                structure on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                induced (as the initial and final structures) by the various incarnations of its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity
                homomorphism. Exploiting this shows how to construct final structures out of initial ones and conversely.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+monomorphism"} regular
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subalgebra
                of some
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(S)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                into a
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                is of this form; note however that there may be nonregular subobjects in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                even if all subobjects in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                are regular.
          %h2#familiarly_fibrations Familiarly fibrations
          %p
            The theory of topological functors can be developed along the lines of Grothendieck’s theory of fibrations, where
            %em cartesian morphisms
            are replaced by
            = succeed "." do
              %em cartesian families
            %em fibration
            if it creates cartesian morphisms and cartesian morphism compose”, there is the definition “A functor is
            %em topological
            if it creates cartesian families and cartesian families compose”.
